/**
 * AddALevelWords.gs — a one-off import. Run it once, then delete this file.
 *
 * Adds the A Level Chemistry and Maths vocabulary from the Obsidian vault as
 * words in two folders, "A Level Chem" and "A Level Math". Each entry carries
 * the Japanese sense first and the English definition under it, and two
 * example sentences in the note — the kind of sentence the term appears in on
 * an Edexcel paper.
 *
 * How to run it
 *   1. Paste this file into the same Apps Script project as Code.gs — it uses
 *      the helpers there, so Code.gs must already be the current version.
 *   2. Pick addALevelWords in the function list and press Run.
 *   3. Read the log for the counts.
 *
 * Safe to run twice: a word already in the same folder is skipped rather than
 * added again, and nothing that is already in the sheet is modified. Every
 * row is written in one go, so the whole import is a single write.
 */

