   'Give your answer to three significant figures.\nKeep full accuracy until the end, then round to significant figures.'],
  ['Exact Answer', 'Expression',
   '厳密な値。根号・分数・π・対数のまま答える。小数に直してはいけない。\nLeave the answer as a surd, fraction, π or logarithm. Do not convert to a decimal.',
   'Give your answer as an exact answer in terms of π.\nFind the exact answer, leaving it in surd form.'],
  ['Give Your Answer in Simplest Form', 'Expression',
   '最も簡単な形で答えよ。共通因数を約分し、分母を有理化し、同類項をまとめる。\nCancel every common factor, rationalise denominators, and collect terms.',
   'Give your answer in simplest form.\nSimplify fully, giving your answer in simplest form.'],
  ['Given That', 'Expression',
   '〜であるとき。前提として使ってよい情報を導入する。ひとつひとつが別の手がかりであり、配点にもなる。\nIntroduces the information you are allowed to assume. Each given that is a separate piece of data.',
   'Given that the curve passes through (2, 5), find the value of k.\nGiven that x > 0, solve the equation.'],
  ['In Terms Of', 'Expression',
   '〜を用いて表せ。指定された文字だけで答えを書く。小数や他の変数は使わない。\nYour answer must be written using the named letters only.',
   'Find the area in terms of x.\nExpress y in terms of x and k.'],
  ['Let', 'Verb',
   '〜とおく。問題が名前をつけていない量に自分で文字を割り当てる。使う前に単位まで含めて一文で定義する。\nHow you introduce your own letter for a quantity the question has not named.',
   'Let x be the length of the shorter side, in metres.\nLet n be the number of terms in the series.'],
  ['The Set of Values', 'Expression',
   '値の集合。不等式の答え。ひとつの数ではなく範囲であり、不等号を使って書く。\nThe answer to an inequality: not a single number but a range, written with inequality signs.',
   'Find the set of values of x for which the curve is above the line.\nGive the set of values in set notation.'],
  ['The Range of Values', 'Expression',
   '定数の取り得る範囲。未知数が変数ではなく係数のときに使い、条件を満たす定数の範囲を答える。\nUsed when the unknown is a parameter rather than the variable — the values of a constant for which a condition holds.',
   'Find the range of values of k for which the equation has no real roots.\nState the range of values of a.'],
  ['Using the Model', 'Expression',
   'モデルを用いて。与えられた仮定の範囲内で答えよという指示。後の小問でモデルの限界を問われることが多い。\nAnswer inside the assumptions you were given; the phrase also warns that the model is not reality.',
   'Using the model, find the population after 10 years.\nUsing the model, estimate the temperature after 5 minutes.'],
  ['Where k Is a Constant to Be Found', 'Expression',
   '（k は求めるべき定数とする）。答えの形は与えられており、空いた文字の値を求めるのが課題。最後に k = … と明記する。\nThe structure of the answer is given; finding the value of the blank letter is the task.',
   'Show that the equation can be written as y = kx2, where k is a constant to be found.\nAlways finish by writing k = … explicitly.'],
  ['Curve', 'Noun',
   '曲線。方程式のグラフ。ふつう C, C₁, C₂ のように大文字で名前がつけられる。\nThe graph of an equation, usually labelled with a capital letter: C, C1, C2.',
   'The curve C has equation y = x3 – 4x.\nFind the coordinates of the point where the curve crosses the y-axis.'],
  ['Equation of a Curve', 'Expression',
   '曲線の方程式。その曲線上の x と y が満たす関係式。「find an equation for C」は標準形で書けという意味。\nThe relation between x and y that the curve satisfies.',
   'Find an equation of the curve, giving your answer in the form y = f(x).\nWrite down the equation of the curve after the translation.'],
  ['Coordinate Axes', 'Expression',
   '座標軸。x 軸と y 軸。「where the curve cuts the coordinate axes」は x 切片と y 切片のこと。\nThe x-axis and the y-axis.',
   'Show where the curve cuts the coordinate axes.\nLabel the points of intersection with the coordinate axes.'],
  ['Gradient', 'Noun',
   '傾き。直線の傾き、または曲線の各点での傾き。曲線では導関数の値にあたる。\nThe steepness of a line, or of a curve at a point; for a curve it is the value of the derivative there.',
   'Find the gradient of the curve at the point (2, 5).\nThe gradient of the line is –3.'],
  ['Tangent', 'Noun',
   '接線。曲線に1点で接し、その点で曲線と同じ傾きをもつ直線。\nA line that touches a curve at a point and has the same gradient as the curve there.',
   'Find an equation of the tangent to the curve at P.\nThe tangent to a circle is perpendicular to the radius at the point of contact.'],
  ['Asymptote', 'Noun',
   '漸近線。曲線が限りなく近づくが決して達しない直線。数ではなく方程式（x = –3、y = 0）で答える。\nA line the curve approaches but never reaches. Given as an equation, never as a number.',
   'Write down the equations of the asymptotes.\nThe curve has an asymptote at y = 0.'],
  ['Stationary Point', 'Noun',
   '停留点。傾きが0になる曲線上の点（dy/dx = 0）。極大・極小・変曲点のいずれか。\nA point on a curve where the gradient is zero. It may be a maximum, a minimum or a point of inflection.',
   'Find the coordinates of the stationary point.\nDetermine the nature of each stationary point.'],
  ['Stationary Value', 'Expression',
   '停留値。停留点における関数の値（起こる x 座標ではなく y の値）。\nThe value of the function at a stationary point — as opposed to the x coordinate where it happens.',
   'Find the stationary value of y.\nState whether the stationary value is a maximum or a minimum.'],
  ['Minimum and Maximum', 'Expression',
   '極小と極大。2種類の転回点。二次導関数の符号で判定する（正なら極小、負なら極大）。\nThe two kinds of turning point, confirmed by the second derivative: positive → minimum, negative → maximum.',
   'Find the coordinates of the minimum and maximum points.\nShow that the point is a minimum.'],
  ['Point of Intersection', 'Expression',
   '交点。2つのグラフが交わる点。連立して解くことで求める。\nWhere two graphs meet. Found by solving their equations simultaneously.',
   'Find the coordinates of the points of intersection of the line and the curve.\nAt the point of intersection the two equations are equal.'],
  ['Figure', 'Noun',
   '図。問題に印刷された番号つきの図（Figure 1 など）。何を示しているか先に読む。\nThe numbered diagram printed with the question: Figure 1, Figure 2.',
   'Figure 2 shows the curve C and the line l.\nThe shaded region in Figure 1 is bounded by the curve and the x-axis.'],
  ['Circle', 'Noun',
   '円。中心から一定の距離にある点の集合。方程式は (x – a)² + (y – b)² = r²。\nThe set of points a fixed distance from a centre; its equation is (x – a)2 + (y – b)2 = r2.',
   'Find an equation of the circle with centre (3, –1) and radius 5.\nShow that the line is a tangent to the circle.'],
  ['Centre and Radius', 'Expression',
   '中心と半径。円の方程式からそのまま読み取る。接点への半径は接線と垂直。\nRead straight off the circle equation: centre (a, b), radius r.',
   'Write down the centre and radius of the circle.\nFind the centre and radius by completing the square.'],
  ['Perpendicular', 'Adj',
   '垂直な。直交する。2直線では傾きの積が −1、2ベクトルでは内積が0になる。\nAt right angles. For two lines, the product of their gradients is –1.',
   'Find an equation of the line perpendicular to l passing through P.\nShow that OA is perpendicular to OB.'],
  ['Magnitude', 'Noun',
   '大きさ。向きを無視したベクトルの長さ。|ai + bj| = √(a² + b²)。力ならニュートン数。\nThe size of a vector, ignoring direction: |ai + bj| = √(a2 + b2).',
   'Find the magnitude of the resultant force.\nCalculate the magnitude of the vector 3i – 4j.'],
  ['Position Vector', 'Noun',
   '位置ベクトル。定点 O からある点へのベクトル。その点の座標そのものでもある。\nThe vector from a fixed origin O to a point; it doubles as the coordinates of that point.',
   'The point A has position vector 2i + 5j.\nFind the position vector of the midpoint of AB.'],
  ['Fixed Origin', 'Expression',
   '定点（原点）。すべての位置ベクトルを測る基準点 O。\nThe reference point O that all position vectors are measured from.',
   'The particle moves relative to a fixed origin O.\nPosition vectors are measured from the fixed origin.'],
  ['Unit Vectors i and j', 'Expression',
   '単位ベクトル i と j。x 方向・y 方向の長さ1の直交ベクトル。平面のベクトルはこの組合せで書く。\nPerpendicular vectors of length 1 along the x and y directions.',
   'Give your answer in terms of the unit vectors i and j.\nThe velocity is (3i + 4j) m s–1.'],
  ['Logarithm', 'Noun',
   '対数。累乗の逆。log_a x は、a を何乗すると x になるかを表す。\nThe inverse of a power: log to base a of x is the power to which a must be raised to give x.',
   'Take logarithms of both sides.\nSolve the equation, giving your answer as a logarithm.'],
  ['Log Laws', 'Expression',
   '対数法則。log xy = log x + log y、log(x/y) = log x – log y、log xⁿ = n log x。積を和に変える。\nlog xy = log x + log y · log (x/y) = log x – log y · log xn = n log x.',
   'Use the log laws to write the expression as a single logarithm.\nApply the log laws to bring the power down.'],
  ['e and the Natural Exponential', 'Expression',
   'e と自然指数関数。定数 e ≈ 2.718。eˣ は微分しても自分自身になるため、成長・減衰モデルに必ず現れる。\nThe constant e ≈ 2.718; the function ex is its own derivative.',
   'Differentiate y = e2x with respect to x.\nThe natural exponential appears in every growth and decay model.'],
  ['Exponential Model', 'Expression',
   '指数モデル。y = abˣ や y = Aeᵏᵗ で表される現実の状況。変化率が現在量に比例する。\nA real situation modelled by y = abx or y = Aekt, where the rate of change is proportional to the current amount.',
   'Using the exponential model, find the value of P when t = 10.\nExplain why an exponential model is suitable here.'],
  ['Log-linear Graph', 'Expression',
   '片対数グラフ。log P を x に対してプロットすると指数関係が直線になり、傾きと切片から定数が求まる。\nPlotting log P against x turns an exponential relationship into a straight line.',
   'The log-linear graph has gradient 0.3 and intercept 1.2.\nUse the log-linear graph to estimate the values of a and b.'],
  ['Acceleration', 'Noun',
   '加速度。速度の変化率。単位は m s⁻²。v を微分して得られ、F = ma で力と結びつく。\nThe rate of change of velocity, in m s–2. Found by differentiating v, and linked to force by F = ma.',
   'Find the acceleration of the particle at time t = 3 s.\nThe car accelerates uniformly at 2 m s–2.'],
  ['Deceleration', 'Noun',
   '減速度。負の加速度。deceleration の語のあとは正の数で答える。\nSlowing down — a negative acceleration. Quote it as a positive number after the word deceleration.',
   'Find the deceleration of the train.\nThe cyclist decelerates at 1.5 m s–2.'],
  ['Acceleration Due to Gravity', 'Expression',
   '重力加速度。この試験で用いる値は g = 9.8 m s⁻²。\ng = 9.8 m s–2, the value specified for this paper.',
   'Take the acceleration due to gravity to be 9.8 m s–2.\nThe ball falls freely under the acceleration due to gravity.'],
  ['Velocity', 'Noun',
   '速度。向きをもつ速さ。記号 v、単位 m s⁻¹。時間で微分すると加速度になる。\nSpeed with direction, written v and measured in m s–1.',
   'Find the velocity of the particle after 4 seconds.\nThe velocity is negative, so the particle is moving in the opposite direction.'],
  ['At Rest', 'Expression',
   '静止している。速度が0の状態。comes to rest は運動の終わりを示す。\nNot moving — velocity zero. Comes to rest marks the end of the motion.',
   'The particle is initially at rest.\nFind the time at which the car comes to rest.'],
  ['Instantaneous Rest', 'Expression',
   '瞬間的な静止。v = 0 だが運動は続く瞬間。区間内にあると移動距離と変位が一致しない。\nA moment when v = 0 but the motion continues; distance travelled is then not the same as displacement.',
   'Show that the particle is at instantaneous rest when t = 2.\nAt instantaneous rest the velocity changes sign.'],
  ['Particle', 'Noun',
   '質点。質量はあるが大きさをもたない点として扱う物体。回転や寸法を無視できる。\nA body treated as a single point with mass but no size.',
   'The box is modelled as a particle.\nA particle of mass 3 kg rests on a smooth plane.'],
  ['Modelled As', 'Expression',
   '〜としてモデル化される。単純化の仮定を導入する言い回し。仮定はすべて現実とのずれの原因になる。\nThe phrase that introduces each simplifying assumption.',
   'The car is modelled as a particle.\nState one limitation of the box being modelled as a particle.'],
  ['Smooth', 'Adj',
   'なめらかな。摩擦のない。なめらかな面は運動方向に力を及ぼさない。\nFrictionless. A smooth surface exerts no force along the direction of motion.',
   'The plane is smooth, so friction can be ignored.\nThe pulley is modelled as smooth and light.'],
  ['Light Rod', 'Expression',
   '軽い棒。質量が無視でき、変形しないとみなす連結棒。両端で張力が等しい。\nA connecting rod modelled as having no mass and being rigid, so the tension is the same at both ends.',
   'The two particles are joined by a light rod.\nBecause the rod is light, the tension is the same throughout.'],
  ['Tension', 'Noun',
   '張力。ひも・ロープ・けん引棒に生じる引く力。T ニュートンと書く。\nThe pulling force in a string, rope or towbar, written T newtons.',
   'Find the tension in the string.\nThe tension in the towbar is 250 N.'],
  ['Driving Force', 'Expression',
   '駆動力。エンジンが生み出す前向きの力。運動方向に働く。\nThe forward force produced by an engine, acting along the direction of motion.',
   'The driving force of the engine is 2000 N.\nFind the magnitude of the driving force.'],
  ['Resistance to Motion', 'Expression',
   '運動への抵抗。摩擦と空気抵抗を合わせた抵抗力。ふつう一定としてニュートンで与えられる。\nThe total opposing force — friction plus air resistance — usually modelled as constant.',
   'The resistance to motion is modelled as a constant force of 400 N.\nFind the total resistance to motion.'],
  ['Newton', 'Noun',
   'ニュートン。力の SI 単位、記号 N。1 N は質量1 kg に 1 m s⁻² の加速度を与える力。\nThe SI unit of force, symbol N. One newton accelerates 1 kg at 1 m s–2.',
   'Give your answer in newtons.\nThe weight of the particle is 29.4 N.'],
  ['Uniformly', 'Adv',
   '一定の割合で。accelerates uniformly は加速度が一定という意味で、速度時間グラフでは直線になる。\nAt a constant rate. Accelerates uniformly means constant acceleration.',
   'The train accelerates uniformly from rest.\nThe particle decelerates uniformly to rest in 8 seconds.'],
  ['Speed-Time Graph', 'Expression',
   '速さ時間グラフ。縦軸が速さ、横軸が時間。傾きが加速度、面積が移動距離を表す。\nSpeed on the vertical axis, time on the horizontal. The gradient is the acceleration and the area is the distance travelled.',
   'Sketch a speed-time graph for the motion of the car.\nUse the speed-time graph to find the total distance travelled.'],
  ['Distance-Time Graph', 'Expression',
   '距離時間グラフ。縦軸が距離、横軸が時間。傾きが速さ。等速なら直線、加速していれば曲線になる。\nDistance on the vertical axis, time on the horizontal; its gradient is the speed.',
   'The distance-time graph is a straight line, so the speed is constant.\nFind the speed from the gradient of the distance-time graph.'],
  ['Function Notation', 'Expression',
   '関数記法。f(x) は x の関数を表す。x に式を代入すると（f(⅓x) など）グラフが変形する。\nf(x) names a function of x; substituting an expression for x transforms it.',
   'The function f is defined by f(x) = 2x2 – 3.\nUsing function notation, write down the value of f(–1).'],
  ['Vector Notation', 'Expression',
   'ベクトル記法。PQ の上に矢印で P から Q へのベクトル。i, j は直交単位ベクトル。印刷では太字、手書きでは下線。\nPQ with an arrow is the vector from P to Q; i and j are perpendicular unit vectors. Vectors are printed in bold.',
   'Write the displacement in vector notation.\nIn vector notation, the force is (4i – 3j) N.'],
  ['Inequality Symbols', 'Expression',
   '不等号。< 小なり、> 大なり、⩽ 以下、⩾ 以上、≠ 等しくない。\n< less than · > greater than · ⩽ less than or equal to · ⩾ greater than or equal to · ≠ not equal to.',
   'Write your answer using inequality symbols.\nThe inequality symbols show that x is between –2 and 5.'],
  ['Therefore', 'Adv',
   'したがって。記号 ∴。上の行から論理的に導かれる行であることを示す。\nThe symbol ∴, read therefore. It marks the line that follows logically from the ones above.',
   'The discriminant is negative; therefore the equation has no real roots.\nWrite ∴ before your conclusion.'],
  ['Because', 'Adv',
   'なぜならば。記号 ∵。直前の行の根拠を導入する。\nThe symbol ∵, read because or since. It introduces the justification for the step just written.',
   'The curve has a minimum, because the second derivative is positive.\nUse ∵ to introduce the reason for the step.'],
  ['Implies', 'Verb',
   '〜を意味する。記号 ⇒。⇔ は「必要十分」で、両方向に成り立つことを表す。\nThe symbol ⇒, read implies or so. ⇔ means if and only if — the step works in both directions.',
   'x2 = 9 implies x = 3 or x = –3.\nUse ⇔ only when the step is reversible.'],
  ['Q.E.D.', 'Acronym',
   'Q.E.D.（quod erat demonstrandum、「これが示されるべきことであった」）。証明の終わりに書き、求める結果に達したことを示す。\nLatin quod erat demonstrandum — "which was to be demonstrated". Written at the end of a proof.',
   'Write Q.E.D. at the end of the proof.\nThe result is proved, Q.E.D.'],
  ['Hypothesis Test', 'Expression',
   '仮説検定。母集団についての主張を棄却できるだけの証拠が標本にあるかを判断する正式な手続き。\nA formal procedure for deciding whether sample evidence is strong enough to reject a claim about a population.',
   'Carry out a hypothesis test at the 5% level of significance.\nState the conclusion of the hypothesis test in context.'],
  ['Null and Alternative Hypotheses', 'Expression',
   '帰無仮説と対立仮説。H₀ は検定する値、H₁ は疑っている内容。「has decreased」なら片側検定の H₁ になる。\nH0 states the value being tested; H1 states what you suspect instead.',
   'Write down the null and alternative hypotheses.\nH0: p = 0.4, H1: p < 0.4.'],
  ['Level of Significance', 'Expression',
   '有意水準。H₀ を棄却する基準となる確率（ここでは5%）。求めた確率がこれより小さければ有意。\nThe threshold probability for rejecting H0. If your probability is below it, the evidence is significant.',
   'Use a 5% level of significance.\nThe probability is less than the level of significance, so reject H0.'],
  ['p-value', 'Noun',
   'p 値。H₀ が正しいと仮定したとき、観測された結果以上に極端な値が出る確率。有意水準と比べる。\nThe probability of getting a result at least as extreme as the observed one, assuming H0 is true.',
   'Find the p-value for this test.\nThe p-value is 0.032, which is less than 0.05.'],
  ['Binomial Distribution', 'Expression',
   '二項分布。X ~ B(n, p)。成功確率 p の独立な試行を n 回行うときの分布。\nX ~ B(n, p) — n independent trials, each succeeding with probability p.',
   'The random variable X follows a binomial distribution B(20, 0.3).\nState two conditions for a binomial distribution to be a suitable model.'],
  ['Probability Distribution', 'Expression',
   '確率分布。確率変数の取り得るすべての値とその確率を示した表または規則。確率の合計は1になる。\nA table or rule listing every possible value of a random variable with its probability; they must sum to 1.',
   'Complete the probability distribution table.\nShow that the probabilities in the probability distribution sum to 1.'],
  ['Random Variable', 'Expression',
   '確率変数。値が偶然によって決まる量。大文字で表し、その具体的な値は小文字で書く。\nA quantity whose value depends on chance, written with a capital letter; its particular values use the small letter.',
   'The random variable X represents the number of heads.\nFind P(X = 3) for the random variable X.'],
  ['Histogram', 'Noun',
   'ヒストグラム。連続量の度数分布図で、面積が度数を表すため縦軸は度数密度になる。\nA diagram for grouped continuous data where area represents frequency, so the vertical axis is frequency density.',
   'Draw a histogram to represent these data.\nUse the histogram to estimate the number of values above 30.'],
  ['Frequency Density', 'Expression',
   '度数密度。度数 ÷ 階級幅。ヒストグラムの各棒の高さ。\nfrequency ÷ class width — the height of each bar on a histogram.',
   'Calculate the frequency density for each class.\nThe vertical axis shows frequency density, not frequency.'],
  ['Box and Whisker Plot', 'Expression',
   '箱ひげ図。最小値・第1四分位数・中央値・第3四分位数・最大値を示す図。方眼上に正確に描く。\nA diagram showing minimum, lower quartile, median, upper quartile and maximum.',
   'Draw a box and whisker plot for the data.\nCompare the two box and whisker plots.'],
  ['Median', 'Noun',
   '中央値。データを順に並べたときの真ん中の値。箱ひげ図では箱の中の線。\nThe middle value when the data are put in order.',
   'Find the median of the data.\nThe median is shown by the line inside the box.'],
  ['Interquartile Range', 'Expression',
   '四分位範囲。第3四分位数から第1四分位数を引いた値。中央50%の散らばりを表し、箱の幅にあたる。\nUpper quartile minus lower quartile — the spread of the middle 50%.',
   'Calculate the interquartile range.\nThe interquartile range is a measure of spread that ignores outliers.'],
  ['Range', 'Noun',
   '範囲。最大値から最小値を引いた値。最小値と組み合わせれば最大値がわかる。\nLargest value minus smallest value.',
   'Find the range of the data.\nThe range is 18, and the smallest value is 4.'],
  ['Summary Statistics', 'Expression',
   '要約統計量。中央値・範囲・四分位数など、データを短く表す数値の組。生データの代わりに与えられることが多い。\nA short set of numbers describing a data set — median, range, quartiles.',
   'The summary statistics for the data are given in the table.\nUse the summary statistics to draw a box plot.'],
  ['Large Data Set', 'Expression',
   '大規模データセット。Edexcel が学習を前提とする実際の気象データ（Camborne、Hurn など）。背景知識が問われる。\nThe real weather data set that Edexcel expects you to have studied.',
   'The data come from the large data set.\nUsing your knowledge of the large data set, suggest why the value is unusual.'],
  ['Sine Rule', 'Noun',
   '正弦定理。a / sin A = b / sin B = c / sin C。1辺とその対角がわかっているときに使う。\na / sin A = b / sin B = c / sin C — used when you have a side and its opposite angle.',
   'Use the sine rule to find the length of BC.\nApply the sine rule to find angle ABC.'],
  ['Cosine Rule', 'Noun',
   '余弦定理。a² = b² + c² – 2bc cos A。3辺、または2辺とその間の角がわかっているときに使う。\na2 = b2 + c2 – 2bc cos A — used with three sides, or two sides and the angle between them.',
